ation":"CONTRIBUTOR","issue_field_values":[],"type":null,"active_lock_reason":null,"sub_issues_summary":{"total":0,"completed":0,"percent_completed":0},"issue_dependencies_summary":{"blocked_by":0,"total_blocked_by":0,"blocking":0,"total_blocking":0},"body":"### Tested versions\n\nReproducible in 4.6 stable on Linux (deb)\n\n### System information\n\nLinux Mint 22.3 Cinnamon 6.6.5 64-bit \n\n### Issue description\n\n\nWhen toggling off and on the screenreader Godot editor crashes with the following message in the terminal:  \n```\nthread '<unnamed>' (40825) panicked at /home/runner/.cargo/registry/src/index.crates.io-1949cf8c6b5b557f/accesskit_consumer-0.31.0/src/tree.rs:136:13:\nTreeUpdate includes 11 nodes which are neither in the current tree nor a child of another node from the update: [#648372557971611, #648763399995638, #648376852938908, #648776284897529, #659681206864453, #659685501831750, #648445572415660, #648389737840799, #648385442873502, #648368263004314 ...]\n```\n\nFrom what I could gather, accesskit is receiving orphaned nodes, panics, then kills Godot. So I guess there are two issues:  \n1: Godot is sending malformed/partial updates when accesskit no longer has the full tree\n2: I don't think Godot should crash if accesskit does\n\nSystem information:\nLinux Mint 22.3 Cinnamon 6.6.5 64-bit\nLinux Kernel 6.8.0-90-generic\n\nProcessor: Intel© Core™ i5-8300H CPU @ 2.30GHz × 4\nGraphics card: Intel Corporation CoffeeLake-H GT2 [UHD Graphics 630]\nGraphics card: NVIDIA Corporation GP107M [GeForce GTX 1050 Mobile]\n\n### Steps to reproduce\n\n- Open Godot 4.6-stable (linux), doesn't even have to be a project just the project overview\n- Turn on the screenreader\n- Turn off the screenreader\n- Turn on the screenreader\n\n### Minimal reproduction project (MRP)\n\nN/A","closed_by":{"login":"akien-mga","id":4701338,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjQ3MDEzMzg=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/4701338?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/